### Personal AI Agent (Operon) V1 - Phase 2 Authentication & User Domain Tests
### Protocol 24: Deterministic Vertical-Slice Functional Testing (.http)
###
### Usage:
###   1. Start backend server: npm run dev:backend (or node backend/src/server.js)
###   2. Open this file in VS Code and click "Send Request" above any scenario.
###      The response displays immediately in the REST Client panel.
###
### Protocol 17 & 61 Authentication Architecture:
###   Authentication is transported exclusively via HttpOnly, SameSite cookies.
###   Tokens (accessToken, refreshToken) are NEVER exposed in JSON response payloads.
###   VS Code REST Client automatically maintains the session cookie jar for localhost.
###   Executing Scenario 5 (Login) automatically authorizes all subsequent User Domain requests!

@host = http://localhost:4000
@baseUrl = {{host}}/api/v1
@authUrl = {{baseUrl}}/auth
@usersUrl = {{baseUrl}}/users

@mockGoogleCode = mock_code_operon.google.user

@testEmail = operon.architect@example.com
@testPassword = OperonPass123!
@newPassword = OperonNewPass456!

### ============================================================================
### AUTHENTICATION DOMAIN TESTS (/api/v1/auth)
### ============================================================================

### 1. Account Registration (Protocol 32 Minimal Registration - Positive)
# @name registerSuccess
# Expected Response:
#   HTTP/1.1 201 Created
#   {
#     "success": true,
#     "message": "Account registered successfully.",
#     "data": {
#       "user": {
#         "email": "operon.architect@example.com",
#         "firstName": "Operon",
#         "lastName": "Architect"
#       }
#     }
#   }
POST {{authUrl}}/register HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "email": "{{testEmail}}",
  "password": "{{testPassword}}"
}

###

### 2. Account Registration - Duplicate Email Rejection (Conflict)
